# Trend judgment #

Financial performance in 2025 was characterized by a typical "merger and digestive period": the income surge was 37% (mainly from the acquisitions of Atria and Comonwealth), but net profits fell by 18%, and net interest rates were compressed by 360 basis points. This was common after large-scale mergers and acquisitions. The central question was whether the profit margin would recover after the consolidation of the acquisitions.

